@NODE QUICKSTART "Quick Start"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

1) In MAIN, optionally pick a theme; in OPTIONS configure export/quality.
2) Left side: choose Pattern Order (preset or manual) – optionally enable SMART.
3) Left side: Base Melody = Random (or pick one); Derivation = Near/Far for variation.
4) Left side: choose instruments per channel (CH1..CH4).
5) Click GENERATE. After rendering: PLAY.

Tip: For reproducible results: disable NEW SEED EACH GENERATE and enter a SEED number.
Tip: For consistently good results: keep Ralph-Loop enabled (default).
@ENDNODE
@NODE GUI "GUI Overview"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

The GUI has two major areas:
- Left: generation parameters (Order, Melody, Key, Speed/Tempo, Advanced, Instruments) + action buttons.
- Right: tabs MAIN / SAMPLES / OPTIONS.

The project generates 4‑channel MODs (ProTracker compatible), optionally renders WAV previews, and provides a text pattern preview.

Next: @{"Left Sidebar" LINK LEFTPANEL} / @{"MAIN tab" LINK MAINTAB} / @{"SAMPLES tab" LINK SAMPLES} / @{"OPTIONS tab" LINK OPTIONS}.
@ENDNODE
@NODE LEFTPANEL "Left Sidebar"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

@{b}PATTERN ORDER@{ub}
- Dropdown: order list (e.g. 0,1,2,3,4,5). Defines which patterns play in which sequence.
- SMART button: auto-generates a sensible order.
- SMART checkbox: if enabled, ignores manual order and always uses SMART.

@{b}BASE MELODY / MELODY DERIVATION@{ub}
- BASE MELODY: pick a specific melody, Random, or Pure Random (style-consistent mixed random basis).
- Derivation: Random / Near / Far – controls how strongly the song deviates from the base.

@{b}BASE KEY (optional)@{ub}
- Leave empty = random key per song.
- Example: C-2. RND picks a suitable key.

@{b}SPEED / TEMPO@{ub}
- SPEED (ticks per row) and TEMPO (BPM-ish) like in trackers.

@{b}Advanced@{ub}
- SCALE MODE: Auto/Major/Minor/Mixed/… (depends on backend).
- VARIATION: mutation amount (0..100). Higher = more change.
- SEED (optional): deterministic generation; RND picks one.
- NEW SEED EACH GENERATE: when enabled, a new seed is used on each generate (and for batch items).
- BATCH: generate multiple songs sequentially.
- MUTE CH: mute individual channels (1..4).
- STEREO %: stereo width/panning (100 = normal).
- PASSES: internal quality/harmony passes (more = slower, often better).

@{b}INSTRUMENTS (CH1..CH4)@{ub}
- Choose instrument per channel; Octave Span controls the note range (CH3 is often bass).

@{b}Action Buttons@{ub}
- GENERATE: generate song(s) with current settings.
- RE-GENERATE: generate again (seed handling depends on NEW SEED EACH GENERATE).
- PLAY: plays the rendered WAV preview (auto-created when Export WAV is enabled).
- STOP: stops playback; if generation is running, requests cancel.
- OPEN OUTPUT: opens output folder (mods_out).
- OPEN PLUGINS: opens melody_plugins folder.
- REFRESH: reloads melody list (plugins + built-ins).
- ADD AS PLUGIN: exports last generated melody as a plugin.
@ENDNODE
@NODE MAINTAB "MAIN tab"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

The MAIN tab contains:
- Visualizer area (Spectrum / Scopes / Light Organ).
- Status line (Render/Thinking/Ralph) + Harmony score.
- Log window (seeds, Ralph scores, FX injection counts, export errors).
- Pattern Preview (text view) + pattern selector.

Switch visualizer mode: click inside the visualizer area.
@ENDNODE
@NODE SAMPLES "Samples"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

In the SAMPLES tab, per channel (CH1..CH4) you get:
- Instrument label (kept in sync with the left instrument dropdowns).
- Status (Generated / Custom).
- Volume (informational).
- Buttons:
  - PLAY: plays a short preview of the sample.
  - Replace: load a custom WAV file for this channel.
  - Reset: remove custom WAV and go back to the generated sample.

Import WAV (multi): lets you select multiple WAV files at once. The first four files are assigned to CH1..CH4 (in selection order).

Note: Custom WAVs are previewed directly; for MOD export the project still follows classic MOD sample constraints.
@ENDNODE
@NODE OPTIONS "Options"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

@{b}Export@{ub}
- Export WAV: renders a WAV next to the MOD and loads it as preview for PLAY/Visualizer.
- Save params (.txt): writes parameters/analysis as a text file next to the MOD.
- Disable vibrato in samples: disables vibrato in synthesized instrument samples (cleaner tone).
- Fade-out pattern: adds a fade-out at the end.
- Slowdown: optional slowdown mode (backend).

@{b}Compatibility@{ub}
- compat_mode: uses tracker-safe defaults (better compatibility with clone trackers).
- MOD Signature: writes the magic at offset 1080 (e.g., M.K., FLT4, 4CHN).

@{b}Ralph-Loop@{ub}
- Enabled by default. Repeats generation attempts until the target score is reached.
- Target %: target for (Harmony + Melody)/2.
- Max attempts: maximum tries; keeps the best attempt.

@{b}Theme@{ub}
- Theme dropdown + Apply: switches QSS theme. Put custom *.qss into /themes.

@{b}LANGUAGE@{ub}
- UI language (lightweight i18n).

@{b}FX Injection@{ub}
Optionally writes effect commands into empty FX slots (post-processing), e.g.:
  - Insert initial speed/tempo: Fxx
  - Vibrato on melody: 4xy
  - Portamento transitions: 3xx
  - Arpeggio ornaments: 0xy
  - Volume motion: Cxx
  - Note cut: ECx
  - Retrig: E9x
Intensity controls how often/how strong effects are injected.

Note: After each generation the log prints `[fx] injected ...` counters.
@ENDNODE
@NODE VISUALIZER "Visualizer"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

The visualizer uses the rendered PCM preview (WAV) plus a playhead to analyze sliding windows.
Modes (click inside the widget):
- Spectrum Analyzer: 32 bars (log-ish frequency spacing).
- Stereo Scopes: separate waveforms for L/R.
- Light Organ: 4 lamps (Low/Mid/High/Presence) with AGC, attack/decay and peak-hold.

Tip: If you see no movement, make sure a WAV preview exists (Export WAV enabled).
@ENDNODE
@NODE PLUGINS "Plugins"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

Melody plugins are stored in `melody_plugins/`.
Each plugin folder typically contains:
- `melody.txt` (melody/parameter export)
- `info.txt` (description)

OPEN PLUGINS opens the folder.
REFRESH reloads the list.
ADD AS PLUGIN exports the last generated melody into a new plugin folder.

Note: Plugins appear in BASE MELODY together with built-ins.
@ENDNODE
@NODE OUTPUT "Output files"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

Default output folder: `mods_out/` (OPEN OUTPUT).
Per song, you may get:
- `*.mod` (tracker module)
- `*.wav` (preview, if Export WAV enabled)
- `*.txt` (parameters/analysis, if Save params enabled)

Filenames usually include title/seed/key (depending on backend settings).
@ENDNODE
@NODE TROUBLE "Troubleshooting"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

@{b}App does not start (Qt platform plugin / xcb)@{ub}
- Linux: install Qt6 platform plugins (xcb).

@{b}PLAY but no sound@{ub}
- Windows: QtMultimedia should work; verify volume and default audio device.
- Linux: install GStreamer plugins or ensure `paplay`/`aplay` are available.

@{b}Visualizer shows nothing@{ub}
- Visualizer needs PCM preview. Enable Export WAV or render once.

@{b}Song sounds 'wrong' (major/minor clash)@{ub}
- Pick the correct SCALE MODE (Major/Minor).
- The project applies a conservative scale-lock post-processor (except Mixed).

@{b}FX injection seems inactive@{ub}
- Check log line `[fx] injected ...`.
- Effects are only written into empty FX slots (safety).
@ENDNODE
@NODE FAQ "FAQ"
@{"Home" LINK MAIN} | @{"Contents" LINK TOC} | @{"Quick Start" LINK QUICKSTART} | @{"GUI Overview" LINK GUI} | @{"Options" LINK OPTIONS} | @{"Samples" LINK SAMPLES} | @{"Visualizer" LINK VISUALIZER} | @{"Plugins" LINK PLUGINS} | @{"Troubleshooting" LINK TROUBLE} | @{"FAQ" LINK FAQ}

Q: Why do I see OKTA/FLT8/8CHN signatures if output is 4 channels?
A: These are just tags (magic). 8ch tags may confuse players; they are marked as '8ch tag'.

Q: What exactly does Ralph-Loop do?
A: It regenerates with widely spaced seeds, evaluates Harmony+Melody, and keeps the best attempt.

Q: How do I get maximum variation?
A: Increase VARIATION, set Derivation=Far, use SCALE MODE Auto or Mixed, Stereo % > 100, and enable NEW SEED EACH GENERATE.
@ENDNODE
